// markdown_cheatsheet.templ — issue #565 + #610
// Article editor Markdown syntax cheatsheet popover.
// Reuses the Foldout primitive (issue #264) so the
// trigger + panel + ARIA menu pattern + CSS show/hide +
// JS-managed aria-expanded are inherited. The component
// adds nothing new to the design system; it is a
// pre-wired Foldout whose children are the rows from
// internal/articles.Rows().
//
// Locked design decisions (from RPCI Critique):
//   - Trigger label: "Markdown syntax" with ▾ chevron
//     (matches the Foldout primitive's visual vocabulary).
//   - Panel: a <ul role="menu"> of <li role="none"> rows.
//     Each row carries a primary Insert-at-cursor menuitem
//     (identified by data-md-cheatsheet-insert-key + value)
//     AND a secondary Copy example button (identified by
//     data-md-cheatsheet-copy-key + value). The two buttons
//     are siblings inside the <li>; the Insert menuitem is
//     full-width so the row click inserts, while the small
//     Copy button on the right provides the existing copy-
//     to-clipboard affordance. The live preview cell
//     (issue #610 slice 1) is identified by
//     data-md-cheatsheet-preview-key.
//   - The popover does NOT steal focus from the editor
//     textarea (matches the issue's "unobtrusive" goal).
//     The menuitem buttons are reachable via Tab through
//     the panel; Escape dismisses via the existing
//     Foldout JS handler.
//   - The popover does NOT include a "View full
//     reference" link in v1 — the user manual is the
//     canonical reference; the popover is the
//     in-context summary. A "View full reference" link
//     can ship in a follow-up once we wire a stable
//     user-manual anchor.
package components

import (
	"github.com/valueforvalue/DixieData/internal/articles"
	"github.com/valueforvalue/DixieData/internal/uiids"
)

// MarkdownCheatsheet renders the Article editor's
// Markdown syntax cheatsheet as a Foldout popover. The
// popover is rendered inline in the editor toolbar and
// starts hidden; the JS Foldout handler toggles
// visibility on click + manages aria-expanded.
//
// Issue #610 slice 1: each row ships a live preview of
// the rendered Markdown so the user sees "**bold**" →
// actual <strong>bold</strong> without having to
// translate syntax mentally. The preview is rendered
// server-side via RenderPreview (records.NewMarkdownRenderer)
// and inserted via templ.Raw — safe because the renderer
// runs the same bluemonday pass as the article editor.
//
// Issue #610 slice 3: each row now ships an Insert-at-
// cursor button as the primary row action (was Copy in
// #565) AND retains the Copy example button as a
// secondary affordance. The Insert menuitem carries
// `data-md-cheatsheet-insert-key` + `data-md-cheatsheet-
// insert-value` so the JS initializer can find the
// <textarea id="article-body"> + call
// window.__dixieInsertTextAtCursor. The Copy button is
// unchanged (same data attrs + handler as before).
templ MarkdownCheatsheet() {
	@Foldout("Markdown syntax", uiids.PanelArticleMarkdownCheatsheet, nil) {
		for _, row := range articles.Rows() {
			<li role="none" class="flex items-stretch gap-1 px-1 py-1">
				<button
					type="button"
					role="menuitem"
					class="foldout-menuitem flex-1 rounded-xl px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm text-slate-100 hover:bg-white/10 focus:bg-white/10 focus:outline-none"
					data-md-cheatsheet-insert-key={ row.Key }
					data-md-cheatsheet-insert-value={ row.Example }
					aria-label={ "Insert " + row.Effect + " example at cursor: " + row.Example }
				>
					<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
						<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--theme-accent-strong)]">{ row.Syntax }</span>
						<span class="shrink-0 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">{ row.Effect }</span>
					</div>
					<div
						class="mt-1 truncate text-[11px] text-slate-400"
						data-md-cheatsheet-preview-key={ row.Key }
					>@templ.Raw(RenderPreview(row.Example))</div>
				</button>
				<button
					type="button"
					class="shrink-0 rounded-xl px-2 py-1 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-300 hover:bg-white/10 focus:bg-white/10 focus:outline-none"
					data-md-cheatsheet-copy-key={ row.Key }
					data-md-cheatsheet-copy-value={ row.Example }
					aria-label={ "Copy " + row.Effect + " example to clipboard: " + row.Example }
					title="Copy to clipboard"
				>Copy</button>
			</li>
		}
	}
}
